    (v_topic_id, 'A 72-year-old patient is recovering from a total hip arthroplasty. According to current guidelines for patients at standard risk for deep vein thrombosis (DVT), what is the most appropriate duration for pharmacologic VTE prophylaxis?', '["3 to 5 days", "3 months", "At least 10 to 14 days, up to 35 days", "24 to 48 hours", "6 months"]'::jsonb, 2, 'Current orthopedic guidelines recommend extending pharmacologic venous thromboembolism (VTE) prophylaxis for a minimum of 10 to 14 days, and up to 35 days, following major joint replacement surgery (THA or TKA) to minimize the risk of DVT and pulmonary embolism.'),
